From 04bc2478d380de4fcce8b123de9b13206817e5e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:02:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Touchveil: patches for layer-shika

Squashes the former patches 0001-0005.

- Output names for OutputPolicy at startup: prefetch wl_output metadata
  before creating surfaces so the policy sees connector names (needed on
  Hyprland to pick a monitor by name).
- Keep the output size: remember the current output mode and apply it
  when a surface is created; mode events can now arrive before surfaces
  exist.
- Render on non-Wayland wakeups: treat WouldBlock from
  prepare_read().read() as a no-op so frames still render when a channel
  or timer wakes the loop.
- Animations: own event loop instead of run(None, ..) that redraws about
  every 16 ms while Slint animates, and advance Slint's clock before every
  event-source callback and before dispatching Wayland events, so
  animations neither jump to their end nor finish on their first frame.
- Seat capabilities: create wl_pointer/wl_keyboard only when the seat
  reports them and release them when they go away (requesting them on a
  seat without these devices is a protocol error on wlroots compositors);
  remove the per-surface copy of the pointer that released it for all
  surfaces when one went away.
- Drop slint's unused backend-winit-wayland feature; require slint
  1.18.1 and wayland-backend client_system directly.
- Remove session lock and popup support (not used by Touchveil).
- Fix pedantic clippy findings; comments in English.
